  "final_answer": "I searched Google Flights for a one-way Dublin to Athens trip for 1 adult on Wed, Dec 30, 2026, then read the price graph in the date picker. Prices are in Malaysian ringgits (MYR). The graph only had prices from Nov 7 to Dec 31, 2026. January 2027 and later had none, so I could only analyse that window.\n\n**Your date (Dec 30):** 494 MYR. Dec 29 is 413 and Dec 31 is 516, so leaving a day earlier would save about 81 MYR.\n\n**Cheapest days:**\n- Mon, Nov 16: 175, the cheapest in the whole window.\n- Mon, Nov 9: 250.\n- Mon, Dec 14: 253.\n- Mon, Dec 7: 259.\n- Mon, Nov 30: 272.\n- Mon, Nov 23: 277.\n\n**Most expensive days:**\n- Fri, Dec 18: 1,330.\n- Sat, Dec 19: 1,250.\n- Nov 7 and Dec 27: about 1,150 each.\n- Sun, Dec 20: 1,060.\n\n**Trends:**\n- **November:** Prices swing widely, from 175 to about 1,150. The cheap days are mostly Mondays, plus Thursdays such as Nov 12 (317) and Nov 26 (281).\n- **Early December (1–14):** Prices are mostly 250–640. Dec 14 at 253 is the best day.\n- **Mid to late December (15–28):** Prices rise sharply, mostly 600–1,330. They peak around Dec 18–20 and again on Dec 27.\n- **Dec 29–31:** Prices ease to 413–516. Dec 29 is the cheapest day in the second half of December.\n\nYour Dec 30 fare of 494 is mid-range. It is well below the holiday peak but about 2.8 times the cheapest day (Nov 16).",
